A||||10||TylerB11||Headache at inspection!||||1||
Z||000000||TylerB11||12-18-2001||09:53 PM||||Good Grief. I took my 85GT for inspection today (NJ, Ridgewood). What a freakin spectacle. <P>They have a little rail you walk behind after you pull the car in, that goes the length of the building and comes out where you get your car back. Instead of going to the end where you are supposed to, I waited, expecting the inevitable problems.<P>"Where is the fuel door release?"<BR>I point it out.<BR>So then I start to go "the engine.."<BR>and the guy snaps "I KNOW WHAT I AM DOING!"<BR>so he pops the hood, and is puzzled by the lack of engine. <BR>(meanwhile the emissions tester down the line who I was chatting with is rolling on the ground lauging. he used to own a fiero)<P>So I ask the guy "What ARE you doing? checking my wiper fluid?"<BR>Emissions guy laughs harder.<BR>The guy slams the hood down and goes "where IS the engine?!"<BR>And I respond with "where do you think it is? in my pocket? if its not in the front, it must be....."<BR>Emissions guy: "its in the back, man."<BR>He snaps back "Fine. whatever. How many cylinders is it? 4?"<BR>Me: "no. six."<BR>him: "really? It can't be."<BR>Me: "If you can find the engine you can see for yourself."<P>At this point the emissions guy steps in and starts to tell the guy how to open the decklid and see the engine. At the same time the manager has heard all this ruckus, and comes over and tells me to go the the waiting section, where I belong, and the emissions guy to go back to his station.<P>So now its time to move it to the emissions guy at the emissions dyno. The guy doesn't take the e-brake off, and tries to drive it anyway. I hear the noise of him revving the engine and dropping the clutch with the ebrake on, and I yelled from the waiting area "WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU DOING TO MY CAR?!? TAKE THE BREAK OFF!!"<P>So now the manager and the guy try to get it off. and finally the manager calls for me to come.<BR>He tells me my e-brake "is broken." <BR>Me: "no its not. watch." <BR>I take it off.<BR>He goes "what kind of weird setup is that?"<BR>Me: "The stock one."<P>Well a half hour inspection that is supposed to take under 10 mins finally is completed with the emissions and brake tests.<P>Passed with flying colors.<P>What a freakin ordeal though. Its like they've NEVER seen a fiero or MR2 or something. Geez.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GTFiero1||12-18-2001||10:15 PM||||hahahaha. thats pretty funny. we dont have to dyno ours or anything at the cherry hill inspecton station<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">    <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)<p>[This message has been edited by GTFiero1 (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||12-18-2001||10:19 PM||||A very scary story, that is soo true!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I'm so glad I know my mechanic well enough that I just pay him for the sticker, and drive off!! <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">         <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed  </FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
